  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Crazy Eights. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
    objective: 'Discard all cards from your hand before the other players.',
    gameplay: 'Play follows the Crazy Eights family: match the current card or use a permitted action card to change the state of play. The custom deck introduces seven levels, with later levels adding extra card functions and tactical restrictions.',
    keyRules: [
      'Players try to empty their hand.',
      'Cards must be legally matched or played for their printed special rule.',
      'The seven-level structure gradually increases rule complexity.',
    ],
